          "what should I do when T2080 S1 Pro has EB1L: The robot encountered an error while adding clean water. Task ended/Robot injecting clean water abnormally?",
          "1. Remove the clean water tank from the base station and check the seal ring of the outlet hole to ensure that it is installed correctly. Have the user shine a flashlight on the clean water tank pipe to check whether the pipe inside the clean water tank is damaged.\n\nhttps://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/the-silicone-rubber-sealing-ring-for-clean-water-outlet.png\n\nhttps://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-pipe-of-clean-water-tank.png\n\n2. Fill the water tank with clean water to the maximum water level, then ensure the water tank is securely placed in the base station.\n\n3. Check the robot's water inlet for debris or blockages, then clean with a paper towel or cotton swab.\n\nhttps://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/water-filling-interface.png\n\n4. After the error occurs, remove the robot from the base station and check the rubber plug at the base station's water inlet to see if there is any water. Additionally, check if the rubber plug is damaged or missing.\n\nhttps://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Silicone-for-base-station-water-injection2.png\n\n5. Update the firmware to version 7.0.143 or higher.\n",
